---
/** Technical docs for schema forms and the in-development visual builder. */
import SolutionDocsPage from '../../../../components/solutions/docs-layout/SolutionDocsPage.astro';
import { parseDocMarkdown } from '../../../../content/solution-docs/parse.ts';
import { getSolution } from '../../../../data/solutions/index.ts';

const sections = [
  {
    id: 'install',
    blocks: parseDocMarkdown(`## Install and status

Install the published schema form package with \`pnpm add @texuli/forms\`. The package is in development (pre-1.0). The visual builder is branch-only while it is in development and is planned for the next release.

Import the base theme stylesheet once in your application. \`SchemaForm\` renders the validated schema using Texuli controls.

\`\`\`svelte
<script lang="ts">
import { SchemaForm, validateFormSchema } from '@texuli/forms';

const result = validateFormSchema({
  title: 'Workshop request',
  fields: [{ name: 'email', type: 'email', label: 'Email address', required: true }],
});
</script>

{#if result.ok}<SchemaForm form={result.form} />{/if}
\`\`\``),
  },
  {
    id: 'schemas',
    blocks: parseDocMarkdown(`## Schemas, conditions and steps

Schemas use closed field types, named formats, validation rules and expression data. Conditions use \`when.show\`, \`when.require\` and \`when.enable\`; expressions are evaluated by the bounded language from \`@texuli/core/expression\`. Multi-step schemas group fields into steps, and hidden or disabled fields are excluded from validation and submission.

Validate the schema before rendering. The validator returns either a compiled form or issues that identify invalid members and relationships.`),
  },
  {
    id: 'drafts',
    blocks: parseDocMarkdown(`## Drafts and host storage

Draft storage belongs to the application. Pass a storage adapter to keep draft behavior under host control. The demo uses fictional \`example.com\` data and keeps its draft in the page session; it sends nothing to a server.

Restored values are checked against the current schema. Credential fields are excluded from drafts by default.`),
  },
  {
    id: 'builder',
    blocks: parseDocMarkdown(`## Visual builder

The in-development \`@texuli/forms/builder\` subpath exports \`FormBuilder\`. It provides a field palette, a keyboard and pointer sortable canvas, a field inspector, a live schema form preview and a schema JSON view. The builder API is available in the repository branch and is planned for the next release.

The builder edits a flat, single-page field list. It does not preserve a multi-step or section layout when editing; use it to author a flat schema and add advanced layout data in your application code.`),
  },
];
---

<SolutionDocsPage
  entry={getSolution('forms')}
  title="Forms docs"
  description="Install and use @texuli/forms schemas, conditions, steps and drafts. The visual builder is in development and is planned for the next release."
  {sections}
/>
